# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-paulice` package. We use [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) to detect errors during execution of a Clifford circuit, then postselect only samples for which no error was detected. For a more explanatory end-to-end workflow that quantifies the fidelity improvement, see the [in-depth tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh kerja minimal dari paket `qiskit-paulice`. Kita pakai [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) untuk mendeteksi error saat eksekusi Clifford circuit, lalu postselect hanya sampel yang tidak terdeteksi errornya. Untuk alur kerja end-to-end yang lebih lengkap dan mengukur peningkatan fidelity, lihat [tutorial mendalam](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Workflow steps**\n"
"1. Prepare the inputs: a Clifford payload circuit, the target/ancilla qubits to host checks, and a noise model.\n"
"2. Find good spacetime Pauli checks and add them to the circuit.\n"
"3. Sample the checked circuit.\n"
"4. Postselect only the samples for which no error was detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah-langkah alur kerja**\n"
"1. Siapkan input: sebuah Clifford payload circuit, qubit target/ancilla untuk menampung check, dan sebuah noise model.\n"
"2. Cari spacetime Pauli checks yang bagus dan tambahkan ke circuit.\n"
"3. Lakukan sampling pada circuit yang sudah dicek.\n"
"4. Postselect hanya sampel yang tidak terdeteksi errornya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"
msgstr "1. Siapkan input {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`add_pauli_checks` takes a Clifford **circuit** ending in measurements (or, with the `stabilizers` kwarg, one with no measurements, as in the [spacetime codes guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), the **target qubits** that will be used to implement checks, and a **noise model** used to score candidate checks. Here we build a shallow random Clifford circuit, lay it out on a 1D chain of physical qubits on `ibm_boston`, pair each payload qubit with a neighboring ancilla (so a check needs no SWAP gates), and infer a rough depolarizing noise model from backend benchmark data.\n"
msgstr "`add_pauli_checks` menerima sebuah Clifford **circuit** yang diakhiri dengan pengukuran (atau, dengan kwarg `stabilizers`, circuit tanpa pengukuran, seperti di [panduan spacetime codes](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), **qubit target** yang akan dipakai untuk mengimplementasikan check, dan **noise model** yang dipakai untuk menilai kandidat check. Di sini kita membuat Clifford circuit acak yang dangkal, menempatkannya pada rantai 1D qubit fisik di `ibm_boston`, memasangkan setiap qubit payload dengan ancilla tetangganya (jadi sebuah check tidak butuh gate SWAP), dan menyimpulkan noise model depolarizing kasar dari data benchmark backend.\n"

